# Hetzner Storage Box SSH host keys — the PIN behind `StrictHostKeyChecking
# yes` in the ssh_config beside this file. Mounted read-only at
# /etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts inside the Backrest container.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: before it, ssh_config said `StrictHostKeyChecking
# accept-new` and the only known_hosts was ~/.ssh/known_hosts in the
# container's WRITABLE LAYER — which is discarded on every `docker compose up`
# that recreates the container (an image bump, a compose edit, an Arcane
# redeploy). So the "trust on first use" happened over and over, and every one
# of those first uses would accept whatever answered. The peer being trusted
# holds credentials that can `forget --prune` every backup this fleet has.
#
# All Storage Boxes share one set of host keys, so this file is not
# per-account and needs no edit when uXXXXXX changes.
#
# ⚠ VERIFICATION (2026-08-31). The keys below were not taken on trust. Hetzner
# publishes FINGERPRINTS, not keys, at
#   https://docs.hetzner.com/storage/storage-box/general/#ssh-host-keys
# so the keys were obtained separately and then checked against the published
# fingerprints with `ssh-keygen -l -f known_hosts`, which reproduced all three
# EXACTLY:
#
#   ED25519  SHA256:XqONwb1S0zuj5A1CDxpOSuD2hnAArV1A3wKY7Z3sdgM
#   RSA      SHA256:EMlfI8GsRIfpVkoW1H2u0zYVpFGKkIMKHFZIRkf2ioI
#   ECDSA    SHA256:oDHZqKXnoMtgvPBjjC57pcuFez28roaEuFcfwyg8O5c
#
# A fingerprint is a hash of the key, so matching all three is proof of
# authenticity, not corroboration — provenance of the key text does not matter
# once the hash agrees with the vendor's published value.
#
# TO RE-VERIFY, or after a Hetzner host-key rotation:
#   ssh-keygen -l -f stacks/backrest/known_hosts        # compare to the docs
#   ssh-keyscan -p 23 uXXXXXX.your-storagebox.de        # what the box serves
# and only then edit this file. A MISMATCH IS NOT A ROTATION UNTIL THE DOCS
# PAGE SAYS SO — that is exactly the alarm this pin exists to raise.
#
# Both key forms are listed because ssh looks up the port it dialled:
# `[host]:23` when Port is 23 (the Storage Box default and what ssh_config
# sets), bare `host` when it is 22.
